# calls-arith.c compiled with -g gives the same transcript as without -g, at
# -O0 and at -O2 (Milestone 4, review-r2 findings 1 and 3; Milestone 7,
# review-r1 finding 3). The -O2 build covers the two Milestone-4 failures,
# which need -O1 or above: with -g at -O1 and above clang turns on call-site
# info (EmitCallSiteInfo), which the MSIL call lowering must keep in step when
# it splits and recombines a call ('Call site info was not updated!'), and
# every x86_64 triple defaults to instruction-referencing variable locations,
# whose LiveDebugValues assumes the allocated physical registers that MSIL
# never has (main's named integer locals, such as one, seven and big, carry
# #dbg_value records). The -O0 build is the mode in which every parameter and
# local is a #dbg_declare of a frame slot, which static frames (M7) make
# reachable. The expected transcript is calls-arith.expected, which
# update-expected.py generates for calls-arith.c; calls-arith.c runs the same
# composite without -g.
# The test is a %{msil_prog} composite of calls-arith.c with %{msil_copts}
# -g and %{msil_expect} calls-arith (plan 5.12.3, 5.12.13 'obj variants'), so
# it builds as the leg's pipeline builds a program (clang -c -g and msil-ld
# under obj, the default, and asm; clang -flto -c -g and the LTO link under
# lto) at the leg's levels (msil_opt_levels: -O0 and -O2 by default) and
# gets every leg of a composite: verification, jitall, the run against
# calls-arith.expected, msil_also_run's runtimes (.NET 10 and .NET 8 with
# DOTNET_TieredCompilation=0 in net8; WSL .NET 8 and .NET 10 with
# TieredCompilation=0 on the Linux triple in wsl-net10), the native oracle
# (calls-arith.c built natively with -g), the round trip and the .NET
# Framework run. Under asm (the asm-oracle leg) Phase 1's route runs too:
# clang -S -g and ilasm -dll at -O0 and -O2, so the text AsmPrinter meets the
# same debug records.
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %S/calls-arith.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_copts} = -g
# REDEFINE: %{msil_expect} = %S/calls-arith
# RUN: %{msil_prog}

# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -O0 -g -S %S/calls-arith.c -o %t.S.O0.il %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %ilasm -dll -output=%t.S.O0.dll %t.S.O0.il %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %msil_verify %t.S.O0.dll %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm && msil-jitall %{ %msil_jitall %t.S.O0.dll %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %msil_exec --expect %S/calls-arith --out %t.S.O0.out %t.S.O0.dll %}

# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -O2 -g -S %S/calls-arith.c -o %t.S.O2.il %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %ilasm -dll -output=%t.S.O2.dll %t.S.O2.il %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %msil_verify %t.S.O2.dll %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm && msil-jitall %{ %msil_jitall %t.S.O2.dll %}
# RUN: %if msil-pipeline=asm %{ %msil_exec --expect %S/calls-arith --out %t.S.O2.out %t.S.O2.dll %}
